From d5d0e35660e00049f22716a778cb2f5bf14c4a60 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slopdealer <326519127+slopdealer@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 15:53:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 46/49] Red team fix 5: nothing is heard of the reads of the
 lock wait unless they are used

The reads a command starts during the lock's settle delay go through the
retrying backend, which reports errors, retries and successes on stderr at
once. A failed index listing of the wait was therefore printed even when the
lock was then refused, where stock, which reads nothing before the lock is
confirmed, prints the lock error only.

The retrying backend can now hold its reports for the operations of a
context (retry.WithHeldReports). The index load of the wait runs on such a
context. Its reports are shown when the index of the wait is kept or
extended, at the point where the command loads the index, in place of what
stock's load would report there. They are dropped when the lock is refused
and when the reads are discarded after confirmation: stock makes no such
reads then, or the load that replaces them reports for itself. The snapshot
listing of the wait is only compared and never used, so its reports are
always dropped. Progress was already held back the same way.

Tests: TestRefusedLockShowsNoWaitDiagnostics (seat 1 R3, carried in; the
restore command, production 200 ms delay) fails before this commit and
passes after. TestWaitDiagnosticsFollowTheUseOfTheReads covers kept,
refused and discarded reads; TestHeldReports covers the holder.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
